          "annotations": [],
          "logprobs": [],
          "text": "{\"occurrence_id\":\"hamsun-pan-0ca06d8ebe15d3db\",\"core_classification\":{\"label_support\":{\"truth_conditional\":4,\"performative\":0,\"exclamatory_reflexive\":0,\"other\":0},\"confidence\":0.92,\"analysis\":\"Edvarda directly avows that she loves the narrator. The declaration responds to his self-deprecating suggestion that God should reward her for accepting him, and principally presents her loving state as true. It does not itself undertake a commitment. Although emotionally intense and preceded by a broken-off phrase, the text does not positively present the words as involuntary or reflex-like rather than as a passionate avowal.\",\"ambiguity\":\"The aposiopesis before the declaration gives it some outburst-like coloring, but intensity, tears, and sudden physical affection can be represented as delivery and context without assigning independent E force.\"},\"other_diagnosis\":{\"tpe_failure\":null,\"core_not_context\":null},\"utterance_status\":{\"status\":\"direct\",\"description\":\"Edvarda directly says “Jeg elsker dig så!” (“I love you so much!”) to the narrator during their conversation.\"},\"contextual_interpretation\":\"Edvarda’s avowal counters the narrator’s transactional and self-abasing framing of her affection as something for which God must reward her. Her tears, immediate embrace, and passionate kiss strongly frame the assertion as emotionally sincere and intense, but they do not by themselves make its core force expressive/reflexive. No explicit promise or relational undertaking is made by these words.\",\"evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"ev1\",\"source\":\"local_text\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"“Det lydde så underlig at Gud vilde lønne mig for det. Du sier slikt noget som .... Jeg elsker dig så!”\",\"supports\":\"The declaration answers Edvarda’s objection to his claim that God should reward her and directly avows her love, strongly supporting T.\",\"confidence\":0.98},{\"evidence_id\":\"ev2\",\"source\":\"local_text\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"Immediately afterward, “Hun fløi mig med en gang om halsen ... og kysset mig hæftig” (she throws her arms around his neck and kisses him passionately).\",\"supports\":\"The physical response corroborates strong romantic affect and contextual intensity, while not independently establishing P or reflex-like E force.\",\"confidence\":0.97},{\"evidence_id\":\"ev3\",\"source\":\"local_text\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"The narrator has just told her, “jeg er så ganske din, så voldsomt din,” and notices tears in her eyes before her reply.\",\"supports\":\"The exchange situates her words as an emotionally charged reciprocal avowal; her utterance itself nevertheless contains no explicit undertaking.\",\"confidence\":0.95}],\"background_knowledge\":{\"used\":false,\"familiarity\":\"none\",\"confidence\":null,\"contribution\":null},\"ontology_assessment\":{\"fit\":\"natural\",\"diagnosis\":\"T naturally captures the core avowal. The surrounding emotional intensity is contextually important but creates no residual core-force pressure requiring E or O.\",\"candidate_recurrent_dimension\":null},\"notes\":null}"
        }
